jacent edge squares (C8 is not valid as there is no anchor; B8 and D8 are also not enabled).\n\nReason: I chose (C, 7) because it is the safest and most strategic move available. It minimizes the number of flipped pieces (only 1), which limits the opponent\'s counter-play options. Furthermore, it places a piece on the board without surrendering corner or edge control to the opponent, unlike the other valid moves which expose edges or corners.\n\nAnswer: (C, 7)'}
